# =============================================================================
# Trivy ignore list — DocuGardener container scan (security-scan.yml)
# =============================================================================
# Defensive net for `linux-libc-dev` (Linux kernel userspace HEADERS).
#
# Why these are ignored:
#   * `linux-libc-dev` ships ONLY C header files (/usr/include/linux/*.h). It
#     contains no executable code and NO running kernel. The container always
#     runs on the host kernel (VPS / colima), never on anything from this
#     package, so these kernel CVEs are not reachable here.
#   * The package entered the image transitively via libc6-dev (pulled by the
#     -dev build packages). The structural fix in docker/Dockerfile removes it
#     from the production stage entirely (runtime shared libs only), so after
#     the next image rebuild + deploy these IDs will no longer appear at all.
#   * This file is the belt-and-suspenders layer: it keeps the Security tab
#     clean in the window before the rebuilt image is deployed, and absorbs any
#     freshly-disclosed linux-libc-dev kernel-header CVE in the same class.
#
# Trivy reads `.trivyignore` from the scan working dir automatically — no
# workflow change required. Review/prune once the rebuilt image is confirmed
# live (the structural fix makes these entries dead no-ops). Added 2026-06-24.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

